# Boolean fit checks — never printed or sliced, rendered by gate.sh.
# fit-mate: the production male thread ∩ the production collar solid, seated
#   as the assembly seats (rim on the flange face, phases aligned by the
#   shared lead_in offset). Zero facets = the printed thread mates at
#   thread_tol.
# fit-mate-ctrl: the same boolean with the collar a quarter turn off — at
#   starts = 2 that parks every rib half a pitch from every groove, real
#   volumetric overlap. The mandatory negative control: if this ever renders
#   empty, the empty check above is proving nothing.
fit-mate       empty
fit-mate-ctrl  interferes
